        <<< Change Log >>>
07/18/2026
	* Completed collisional abosorption model update
	** nu_col(Tc) option is added in cold,lkplasma (discussed in 07/07)
	** Tc option is kept the same as before. (See 07/07 log)
07/15/2026
	* improved hot plasma dielectric tensor to support two interfaces
             epsilonr_pl_hot_std(w, B, temps, denses, masses, charges, Te, ne,
                                 npara, nperp, nhrms, terms, use_eye3)
             epsilonr_pl_hot_std(w, B, temps, denses, masses, charges, Te, ne,
                                 npara, nperp, nhrms, terms, use_eye3, nucol)
        ** nucol is collision frequency to introduce anti-herminain part by
	   damping the dielectric current. W/o setting it, nucol is set to zero.


07/07/2026
	* improved cold plasma collision model. One can directly specify array
	of collision frequecies for electrons and ions.

	** w/o col. : no collision
	** Tc : Tc is used to evaluate electron-ion collsion frequecy and used as f_col for all spiecies.
	** nu_col(Tc) : collision frequency is computed by using Tc as electron temperature.
	** nu_col : directly setting nu_col for all species
	** nu_col(array) : setting nu_cols indpendently for each species. Must be array
	                   size of 1 + number of ions. First element is for electrons.

02/10/2026
	* created from PetraM-RF module by separating RF physics for plasma waves
